# The Edgegap "Containerize with Docker" tool (Assets/Mirror/Hosting/Edgegap) uses the whole
# project root as the build context, but the Dockerfile only COPYs the Builds/<name> server
# output. Excluding everything else keeps huge/constantly-churning folders like Library/
# (Unity rewrites Library/PackageCache on every package resolve) out of the context, which
# also caused a stale-path "resolve ... GetFileAttributesEx" Docker build failure.
Library/
Temp/
Logs/
obj/
.git/
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
UserSettings/
Builds/*/BurstDebugInformation_DoNotShip/
